          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhíbān is built from zhí 'to meet, to hold' and bān 'a turn', both inherited from Middle Chinese, driH and paen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to hold' and 'to meet with' and the second 'to hand out tokens'. The sense 'a shift' is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
