        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 保安",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "保安 — bǎo'ān — \"security guard\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "小区门口有两个保安 xiǎoqū ménkǒu yǒu liǎng ge bǎo'ān — There are two security guards at the gate of the estate."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 保 (bǎo) — nine strokes in three pieces: the person piece 亻, then 口 high on the right over a tree of four strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "保安 (bǎo'ān) is built from 保 'to keep' and 安 'calm', both inherited from Middle Chinese, pawX and 'an (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to guard' and 'to keep safe': keeping the peace, and then the person who does it."
            }
          ]
        },
